title: consuming another's changes, as skg stood on 2026-11-12
pid: fc5df1db-2e18-4337-b8c7-7e238647b46a
body: |2-
  What it was like for me, Ed, to read what Jeff changed in his public skgrepo over the week to 2026-11-12, from my own server, where his skgrepo is foreign. The reader was the command-line client, not Emacs. Git told me what had changed (three commits, and 23 files changed since); every attempt below then used skg alone.
  One headline per wish, the most wanted first. Under each, the attempt that produced it: what I tried, what I expected, what happened.
  Jeff's own sketch of how it should go is [[id:be02e08b-2913-447e-ae16-cf7043ec477a][how to consume subscriptions]]; the last headline compares the two.
